This license applies to AeroTune, including its source code, analyzer logic, parser logic, comparison logic, tuning recommendation logic, user interface, documentation, project materials, branding, and related files unless a specific file states otherwise.

AeroTune is source-available, not open-source software.

Access to the source code does not grant ownership of the project and does not grant permission to copy, resell, rehost, redistribute, commercialize, or reuse AeroTune in another product without written permission from Christopher Bostrom.

1. PUBLIC WEB USE

The public AeroTune web version may be used to analyze your own FPV drone logs through the official AeroTune website when available.

Public web use is allowed for personal, educational, and non-commercial FPV tuning review.

You may not abuse, scrape, overload, mirror, clone, rehost, or automate against the public AeroTune website in a way that harms the service, bypasses access limits, or copies the service into another product.

2. APPROVED SUPPORTER LOCAL ACCESS

Approved AeroTune supporters may be granted access to a private local analyzer repository through Patreon or another official AeroTune support channel.

Approved supporter access allows you to:

- View the AeroTune source code.
- Clone the private supporter repository.
- Run AeroTune locally on your own machine.
- Analyze your own Betaflight Blackbox logs.
- Use AeroTune for personal, non-commercial FPV tuning review.
- Receive access to updates while your access remains active and the supporter repository remains maintained.

Approved supporter access does not allow you to:

- Resell AeroTune.
- Redistribute AeroTune.
- Rehost AeroTune as your own website, app, API, or paid service.
- Publish the private source code.
- Share private repository access with other people.
- Sublicense AeroTune.
- Copy AeroTune logic into another project.
- Sell AeroTune analysis as your own software product.
- Remove attribution, copyright notices, license notices, or ownership notices.
- Claim AeroTune or derivative work as your own original project.

3. PATREON AND SUPPORTER TERMS

A Patreon pledge, donation, supporter tier, or paid support option does not transfer ownership of AeroTune.

Supporter access is personal to the approved supporter account.

Lifetime local repository access, when offered, means access for the life of the supported AeroTune local repository while the supporter follows these license terms, the repository remains available, and AeroTune remains maintained by the original maintainer.

Access may be revoked if these terms are violated, if access is abused, if private files are redistributed, or if AeroTune is copied into another public or paid product without permission.

Lower support tiers may include Discord or community access only. Local repository access is only included when specifically offered through an approved support tier or direct written permission.

4. LOG REVIEW AND TUNING SUPPORT

AeroTune log reviews, written recommendations, Discord discussion, voice calls, video calls, or full drone support are educational and advisory.

No tuning recommendation is guaranteed to make a drone safe, perfect, faster, more efficient, or crash-proof.

Every FPV drone build is different. Frame stiffness, motor size, prop size, ESC firmware, gyro noise, filtering, battery condition, mechanical condition, pilot style, and environment can all affect flight behavior.

You are responsible for your own aircraft, tuning decisions, testing process, flight safety, and compliance with applicable rules or laws.

Always test carefully, make small changes, check motor temperature, inspect the aircraft mechanically, and revert changes if the drone sounds noisy, motors get hot, or flight behavior becomes unsafe.

