Without prior written permission from Christopher Bostrom, you may not:

- Copy AeroTune into another public repository.
- Copy AeroTune into another private commercial repository.
- Repackage AeroTune under another name.
- Sell AeroTune or modified AeroTune builds.
- Rehost AeroTune as a competing web service.
- Offer AeroTune as a paid SaaS, API, app, or tuning platform.
- Use AeroTune branding, name, logo, UI identity, documentation, or project materials in a way that suggests ownership, partnership, endorsement, or official affiliation.
- Remove or alter copyright, attribution, license, or ownership notices.
- Publish derivative works based on AeroTune source code, analyzer logic, parser logic, comparison logic, tuning recommendation logic, UI structure, documentation, or project materials.

